  "name": "VITAMIN B6",
  "code": "2869",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>1) The main circulating forms of Vitamin B6 are pyridoxal phosphate (PLP), pyridoxal(PL) &amp; pyridoxic acid(PA).<br>2) The active form in the body is PLP.It acts as a coenzyme for many enzymes in the body &amp; is involved in metabolism of protein, carbohydrates &amp; fats, production of Serotonin &amp; haem &amp; binding of steroid hormones to their receptors.<br>3) Dietary deficiency is uncommon. The common cause of deficiency is ingestion or use of antagonists like cyclosporine, hydrazaline, Isoniazide &amp; penicillamine.<br>4) Sideroblastic anaemias have been described that are responsive to Vitamin B6 administration.<br>5) It may be decreased in pregnancy,lactation,alcoholism,diabetes mellitus, &amp; in an uncommon dependency states.<br>RECOMMENDATIONS :<br>1. Withhold Vitamin B6 supplement for 24hrs before test.<br>REFERENCES :<br>1. Bender DA, Novel functions of Vitamin B6,Proc Nutr Soc,1994,53:625-30.<br>2. Borschel MW,Kirskey A, &amp; Hannemann RE,Effects of Vitamin B6 intake on Growth of Young I infants, \"Am J Clin Nutr,1986,43(1):7-15.</p>",
